{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rUdkvSdBVH2uvbjXFi5tR","type":"tool_result","content":"3-\n4:.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures lint-scanner-fixtures chart-test image-test\n5-\n6-build:\n7-\tCGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags \"$(LDFLAGS)\" -o bin/ard ./cmd/ard\n8-\n9-test:\n10-\tgo test ./...\n--\n30-# Needs Docker and network; not part of `make test`.\n31:cve-fixtures:\n32:\tdocker build -t ard-cve-fixtures internal/roles/scanners/cve\n33-\tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n34:\t  -v \"$$PWD/internal/roles:/roles\" -w /roles ard-cve-fixtures sh testdata/cve/regen.sh\n35-\n36-# Regenerates the real lint scanner fixtures in the pinned image (see\n37-# internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh). Needs Docker; not part of `make test`.\n38-lint-scanner-fixtures:\n39-\tdocker build -t ard-lint-fixtures internal/roles/scanners/lint\n40-\tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n#!/bin/sh\n# Regenerates the REAL fixture cases (both_tools, osv_only, not_called,\n# nested_module, scoped_npm) from real tool runs. Run it inside the pinned\n# image so the tool versions are exactly the Dockerfile's:\n#\n#   make cve-fixtures        # from the repo root; needs Docker and network\n#\n# (it runs: docker run ... -v internal/roles:/roles -w /roles IMAGE\n#  sh testdata/cve/regen.sh). Needs osv-scanner, govulncheck, go and jq on\n# PATH, plus egress to proxy.golang.org, api.osv.dev and vuln.go.dev.\n#\n# Per case it builds a tiny module (or lockfile) under a fixed temp root, runs\n# osv-scanner with the flags `scan` uses, runs govulncheck per Go module, and\n# writes osv.json, gv.jsonl and want.jsonl next to this script.\n#\n# Edits to real output (the only ones):\n#   - osv.json: the temp root in results[].source.path becomes @ROOT@\n#     (the tests turn it into /R); pretty-printed with `jq .`.\n#   - gv.jsonl: each module's govulncheck messages are trimmed to the `config`\n#     message, every `finding`, and the `osv` messages a finding references.\n#     `progress`, `SBOM` and unreferenced `osv` messages (~190 of them, 590 KB;\n#     merge.jq never reads them) are dropped.\n#   - want.jsonl: merge.jq output, exactly as the tests' runMerge produces it.\n#     Review every diff by hand: the golden test cannot tell a correct change\n#     from a regression.\n# The hand-written synthetic cases are never touched; see cve_test.go.\nset -eu\n\nhere=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\nmerge=\"$here/../../scanners/cve/merge.jq\"\nARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\nARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\nARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\n# tini v0.19.0 static, checksums from the release's .sha256sum files.\nARG TINI_VERSION=v0.19.0\nARG TINI_SHA256_AMD64=c5b0666b4cb676901f90dfcb37106783c5fe2077b04590973b885950611b30ee\nARG TINI_SHA256_ARM64=eae1d3aa50c48fb23b8cbdf4e369d0910dfc538566bfd09df89a774aa84a48b9\nRUN set -eu; \\\n    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n      amd64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\"; tini_sha=\"${TINI_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n      arm64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\"; tini_sha=\"${TINI_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n    esac; \\\n    mkdir /out; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/osv-scanner \"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/download/${OSV_SCANNER_VERSION}/osv-scanner_linux_${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${osv_sha}  /out/osv-scanner\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/tini \"https://github.com/krallin/tini/releases/download/${TINI_VERSION}/tini-static-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${tini_sha}  /out/tini\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    chmod 0755 /out/osv-scanner /out/jq /out/tini\n\n# The final image keeps the Go toolchain (govulncheck loads packages with it);\n# git and ca-certificates are already in the golang image.\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE}\nARG VERSION=dev\nARG REVISION=unknown\nCOPY --from=build /out/ard /usr/local/bin/ard\nCOPY --from=build /out/govulncheck /usr/local/bin/govulncheck\nCOPY --from=tools /out/osv-scanner /usr/local/bin/osv-scanner\nCOPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\nCOPY --from=tools /out/tini /usr/local/bin/tini\n# HOME is the pod's PVC (~/.ard state, the repo clone, Go caches). TMPDIR is\n# exec-capable for the cve scan's toolchain downloads. GOTOOLCHAIN=local: the\n# scan switches toolchains itself.\nENV HOME=/home/ard \\\n14:command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"ERROR: jq is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\n42:idx=\"$work/oci/blobs/$(jq -r '.manifests[0].digest | sub(\":\"; \"/\")' \"$work/oci/index.json\")\"\n43:platforms=\"$(jq -r '[.manifests[] | select(.platform.os != \"unknown\") | .platform.os + \"/\" + .platform.architecture] | sort | join(\",\")' \"$idx\")\"\n62:  [ \"$(run --entrypoint jq \"$tag\" --version)\" = \"jq-1.8.2\" ] || { echo \"jq: $(run --entrypoint jq \"$tag\" --version)\" >&2; return 1; }\n81:  if [ ! -s \"$scan_out\" ] || jq -e -s 'all(.[]; type == \"object\" and has(\"fingerprint\"))' \"$scan_out\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n96:   && jq -e -s 'length >= 1 and all(.[]; type == \"object\" and (.fingerprint | startswith(\"osv:\")))\n2:osv.dev and vuln.go.dev for the cve scan), never other namespaces, private or CGNAT ranges, or link-local metadata. */ -}}\ndocs/proposal.md:221:**The cve scanner** (`scanners/cve`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program, no build step) merges osv-scanner (all ecosystems) and govulncheck (Go reachability). Its fingerprint is `osv:<advisory>:<man\ndocs/proposal.md:431:  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\ndocs/proposal.md:450:**`ard init` proposes the