{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMjMSVGTw827iUQhNvzj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FvsEUbXuhe9vdN64avDjkk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/mk.txt <<'EOF'\n\n# Regenerates the real lts API fixtures inside the pinned lts image (see\n# internal/roles/testdata/lts/regen.sh). Needs Docker and network; not part of `make test`.\nlts-fixtures:\n\tdocker build -t ard-lts-fixtures internal/roles/scanners/lts\n\tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n\t  -v \"$$PWD/internal/roles:/roles\" -w /roles ard-lts-fixtures sh testdata/lts/regen.sh\nEOF\nsed -n 31,35p Makefile\nsed -i '' '34r /tmp/mk.txt' Makefile\ncat > /tmp/ti.txt <<'EOF'\n# The lts role the same way. It needs network (endoflife.date); empty output and finding lines both pass.\nlts_out=\"$work/lts.out\"\nif run --tmpfs /home/ard:uid=65532,gid=65532,exec --tmpfs /var/tmp:uid=65532,gid=65532,exec \\\n     -v \"$ROOT:/repo:ro\" -w /repo --entrypoint /repo/internal/roles/scanners/lts/scan \"$tag\" >\"$lts_out\" 2>\"$work/lts.err\"; then\n  if [ ! -s \"$lts_out\" ] || jq -e -s 'all(.[]; type == \"object\" and has(\"fingerprint\"))' \"$lts_out\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    pass \"lts scan runs in the image as a host subprocess\"\n  else\n    fail \"lts scan runs in the image as a host subprocess\" \"stdout is not finding JSON lines: $(head -c 300 \"$lts_out\")\"\n  fi\nelse\n  fail \"lts scan runs in the image as a host subprocess\" \"exit $?: $(tail -5 \"$work/lts.err\")\"\nfi\n\nEOF\nsed -i '' '89r /tmp/ti.txt' deploy/test-image.sh\nsed -i '' '/run --entrypoint git \"\\$tag\" --version/i\\\n  run --entrypoint yq \"$tag\" --version | grep -q '\"'\"'version v4\\\\.54\\\\.3$'\"'\"' || { echo \"yq: $(run --entrypoint yq \"$tag\" --version)\" >&2; return 1; }' deploy/test-image.sh\ncat > /tmp/doc.txt <<'EOF'\n**The lts scanner** (`scanners/lts`, a `sh` script plus two `jq` programs and `yq` for Helm, no build step) flags components at or near end of life using the endoflife.date v1 API (`/api/v1/products/<slug>`, one request per referenced product). A component is a product plus a release cycle. Its fingerprint is `eol:<product>:<cycle>` (for example `eol:nodejs:18`), one finding lists every referencing file, and `group` is the product. The human-owned `products.json` maps Docker image names and a few npm packages to endoflife.date slugs (the Alpine image maps to `alpine-linux`); names not in it are skipped with a stderr line. Cycles match generically: a codename's first word (`bookworm`, `jammy`), else the longest dotted prefix of the version. It reads the `toolchain` line (else the `go` directive) of `go.mod`; `engines.node` and table npm dependencies of `package.json` (lowest lower bound of the range); Dockerfile `FROM` lines (`Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.*`, `*.Dockerfile`, `Containerfile`; global `ARG` substitution, registry and digest stripped); and `repository`/`tag` or `image: name:tag` in the `values.yaml` beside each `Chart.yaml`. Severity is `high` at or past end of life, `medium` within 90 days, `low` within 180 days, otherwise no finding. A component referenced only by floors (a `go` directive, `engines.node`, an npm range) is capped at `medium`. Titles carry the date (`Go 1.21: end of life 2024-08-13`), never \"approaching\" or \"past\", because rerate changes only severity. The scan fails closed with nothing on stdout, because an absent finding closes its issue: any API failure (including a 404 for a mapped product, which means `products.json` is stale), a non-JSON response, and a `package.json` or `values.yaml` that cannot be parsed. A missing tool exits 2 (`yq` only when a `Chart.yaml` exists). Paths with a `.git`, `vendor`, `node_modules` or `testdata` segment are skipped. Manifest text reaches the issue body only as cleaned text in code spans (control characters and backticks removed, 200 characters, at most 50 references), and repo text never reaches a URL.\n\nEOF\nn=$(grep -n '^\\*\\*The trufflehog scanner' docs/proposal.md | cut -d: -f1); sed -i '' \"$((n-1))r /tmp/doc.txt\" docs/proposal.md\ncat > internal/roles/testdata/lts/regen.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\n# Regenerates the real endoflife.date fixtures in api/ (go, nodejs, python,\n# debian, ubuntu, alpine-linux, redis, nginx, angular). Run it inside the pinned\n# lts image:\n#\n#   make lts-fixtures        # from the repo root; needs Docker and network\n#\n# Each response is stored as `jq .` output with no other change. api/synthetic.json\n# is hand-written and never touched. Review every diff by hand: the golden tests\n# in lts_test.go use these files, and a changed capture can change their results.\nset -eu\n\nhere=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\nfor p in go nodejs python debian ubuntu alpine-linux redis nginx angular; do\n  curl --proto =https --tlsv1.2 -sS --max-time 30 --retry 2 -f -A ard-lts-scanner \\\n    \"https://endoflife.date/api/v1/products/$p\" | jq . > \"$here/api/$p.json.new\"\n  mv \"$here/api/$p.json.new\" \"$here/api/$p.json\"\ndone\nEOF\nchmod 755 internal/roles/testdata/lts/regen.sh\ngit diff Makefile deploy/test-image.sh | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-120"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152,"cache_read_input_tokens":92792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":152},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df64a9c0-ea4b-43ef-9ca6-e1675383808b","uuid":"53f2e3e9-2090-4fc2-bd02-34e3cad1bc71","timestamp":"2026-11-24T12:11:49.745Z","request_id":"req_011ChMjMSLqJbZ1WxmTUNLEv"}
